---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

title: "Roadmap";
description: "The future direction of the Umi‑Time project and ecosystem.";
---

<Base title="Roadmap">
  <div class="umi-region umi-pad">
    <main class="page page-roadmap">
      <header class="page-header">
        <h1>Roadmap</h1>

        <p>
          Umi‑Time is an open standard, not merely a software project. The
          standard itself already exists; the next challenge is building the
          ecosystem around it.
        </p>

        <p>
          This roadmap outlines the kinds of work that can help Umi‑Time grow
          from a specification and reference implementation into a broader
          community of tools, libraries, educational resources, and
          independent implementations.
        </p>

        <p>
          These milestones are directional rather than prescriptive. New ideas,
          contributors, and opportunities may change the path over time.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- ========================================================== -->
      <!-- Short Term -->
      <!-- ========================================================== -->

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Short‑Term</h2>

        <p>
          The foundation is now in place. The next phase focuses on growing the
          ecosystem and making it easier for others to participate.
        </p>

        <h3>Additional Implementations</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Python implementation</li>
          <li>Rust implementation</li>
          <li>Go implementation</li>
          <li>Java implementation</li>
          <li>C# implementation</li>
          <li>C/C++ implementation</li>
          <li>Swift implementation</li>
          <li>Kotlin implementation</li>
          <li>PHP implementation</li>
          <li>Ruby implementation</li>
          <li>Additional community‑maintained language ports</li>
          <li>Shared conformance and compatibility testing</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Developer Tooling</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Additional formatting and parsing utilities</li>
          <li>Framework integrations and examples</li>
          <li>Reusable web components and widgets</li>
          <li>Reference applications demonstrating real‑world usage</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Documentation & Education</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Expanded tutorials and learning materials</li>
          <li>Additional technical examples</li>
          <li>Visual explanations of core concepts</li>
          <li>Translation and accessibility improvements</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Community</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Welcoming new contributors</li>
          <li>Independent review of the specification</li>
          <li>Community discussion and feedback</li>
          <li>Solving real‑world scheduling and time management problems</li>
          <li>Overcoming adoption and integration challenges</li>
          <li>Third‑party experiments built on Umi‑Time</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- ========================================================== -->
      <!-- Mid Term -->
      <!-- ========================================================== -->

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Mid‑Term</h2>

        <p>
          The goal of this phase is to establish Umi‑Time as a mature open
          ecosystem supported by multiple implementations and independent
          contributors.
        </p>

        <h3>Multi‑Language Ecosystem</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Mature implementations across multiple programming languages</li>
          <li>Shared test suites and interoperability validation</li>
          <li>Implementation guides and conformance resources</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Applications & Integrations</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Desktop widgets and companion applications</li>
          <li>Browser extensions</li>
          <li>Smartwatch and wearable interfaces</li>
          <li>Scheduling and collaboration tools</li>
          <li>Mapping and visualization applications</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Educational Resources</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Independent tutorials and articles</li>
          <li>Videos, talks, and presentations</li>
          <li>Classroom and educational use cases</li>
          <li>Community‑created learning materials</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Standard Maturity</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Stable long‑term specification releases</li>
          <li>Independent implementations validating the standard</li>
          <li>Archival publication and citation support</li>
          <li>Long‑term maintenance and governance processes</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- ========================================================== -->
      <!-- Long Term -->
      <!-- ========================================================== -->

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Long‑Term</h2>

        <p>
          The long‑term vision is a world in which a shared planetary time can
          coexist alongside local experience of the day.
        </p>

        <h3>Broad Availability</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Support across many platforms and programming environments</li>
          <li>Multiple mature, independently maintained implementations</li>
          <li>Integration into a wide range of software and devices</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Community Sustainability</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Project stewardship extending beyond any single contributor</li>
          <li>Independent maintainers and implementers</li>
          <li>Long‑term preservation of the specification</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Recognition & Adoption</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Growing awareness of Umi‑Time as an open standard</li>
          <li>Routine use in communities that coordinate globally</li>
          <li>Independent educational and research references</li>
          <li>Continued exploration of universal time representation</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- ========================================================== -->
      <!-- Closing -->
      <!-- ========================================================== -->

      <section class="section">
        <h2>How to Help</h2>

        <p>
          The most valuable contributions are not necessarily changes to the
          specification itself. New implementations, documentation, examples,
          educational content, integrations, visualizations, and community
          discussion all help strengthen the Umi‑Time ecosystem.
        </p>

        <p>
          If any of these goals interest you, visit the
          <a href="/contributing">Contributing</a> page and join the discussion.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Base>